From 4c22fec581d5cac5f6e4b0481d141d9c919c7bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 13:38:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 601/913] dts: stm32: set the GPIOs used for wake-up as secure
 on stm32mp135f-dk

Set these GPIOs as secure to avoid the non secure to use them and
provoke spurious interrupts.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git e10635df182baa5eed867eed92cdbd48311628ce dts: stm32: set the GPIOs used for wake-up as secure on stm32mp135f-dk]
Change-Id: I77a65369b4bd24ce5aee1c741317167b8df9eefb
Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/573251
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp135f-dk.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp135f-dk.dts b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp135f-dk.dts
index 863948098..fe09986d4 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp135f-dk.dts
+++ b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp135f-dk.dts
@@ -146,6 +146,14 @@
 	st,protreg = <TZPROT(15)>;
 };
 
+&gpiof {
+	st,protreg = <TZPROT(8)>;
+};
+
+&gpioi {
+	st,protreg = <(TZPROT(2) | TZPROT(3))>;
+};
+
 &hash {
 	status = "okay";
 };
